      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T12:07:16Z",
      "note": "Reviewed Parity's post-mortem, the deployment, initialization, and kill transaction records, archive-node runtime at deployment block 4049249 and the block immediately before the kill, verified historical source, EIP-999, and the commit-pinned reproduction. WalletLibrary 0x863df6bfa4469f3ead0be8f9f2aae51c91a907b4 was deployed at block 4049249 with a 5,903-byte runtime whose hash is 0x15e25447f2cb376d8b0f5c72a2f8053c293dbe32dd1c3a354ce1fdb6dc76dfb4; the same runtime and hash remained at block 4501968 immediately before the incident block. The later initialization transaction called initWallet directly on that uninitialized library and made 0xae7168deb525862f4fee37d987a971b385b96952 its owner; the incident transaction then called kill directly on the same address and executed SELFDESTRUCT. The library is therefore the causal artifact and direct execution target. Its dependent multisig wallets merely hard-code it as their DELEGATECALL destination. Parity reports that losing this shared code blocked 513,774.16 ETH across 587 wallets, plus additional tokens."
    },
